NNOOTTEE
     The rroouuttee66dd utility uses IPv6 advanced API, defined in RFC2292, for com‐
     municating with peers using link-local addresses.

     Internally rroouuttee66dd embeds interface identifier into bit 32 to 63 of link-
     local addresses (fe80::xx and ff02::xx) so they will be visible on inter‐
     nal state dump file (_/_v_a_r_/_r_u_n_/_r_o_u_t_e_6_d___d_u_m_p).

     Routing table manipulation differs from IPv6 implementation to implemen‐
     tation.  Currently rroouuttee66dd obeys WIDE Hydrangea/KAME IPv6 kernel, and
     will not be able to run on other platforms.

     Current rroouuttee66dd does not reduce the rate of the triggered updates when
     consecutive updates arrive.

